acter  after infinity wars opening scene  ultimately makes his arc that much more  interesting the truth is Hulk had been  little more than a pawn and the Avengers  plans up until this point often only  whipped out to save the day when danger  was about to strike his time on Sekar  gave him a taste of freedom and the big  guy liked it co director Joe Russo  explains it best people speculated  whether there was some fear on the  Hulk's part about having a face stay  honest again but I think ultimately what  it is is that he's tired of playing hero  in the lead-up to infinity war Mark  Ruffalo revealed in an interview that  Bruce Banner and the Hulk were headed  for a showdown while the hint seemed to  point toward a violent conclusion the  rest of Hulk's three-part story actually  ended up playing out in an unexpected  way for a character who was so often  used as an explosive plot device or as a  way to entertain smash happy fans the  pivotal moment for Hulk and banner ended  up being relatively quiet not only that  but it actually took place off screen  when audiences caught up with Hulk again  in endgame the instead ran into  Professor Hulk the long-awaited union of  the two personalities was the result of  18 months of lab-based gamma exposure  leading to the perfect combination of  Banner and Hulk I put the brains and the  Brawn together and now they give me best  of both worlds while the transformative  scene itself was originally meant for  infinity war it ended up being the  perfect way to launch the third and  final part of the Hulk's arc as endgame  plays out so twos does the third and  final portion of Hulk's three-part story  arc looking back it's hard to believe  that this is the same character who just  a handful of years earlier had  maintained a successful gladiatorial  career half a galaxy away by endgame  Hulk is refined thoughtful and caring he  even watches his past self smashing his  way through New York City and declares  it  the banner part of 